**0 of 1 DISCRIMINATING builds** have the shipped run missing its
argmax. Quote that denominator, never 36.

A build can test the shipped run only if the two squads differ and
the floorless one was reachable under the floor (differs > 0 and
entered == 0). Where differs == 0 the squads are the same set and
the objectives are equal BY CONSTRUCTION; where entered > 0 the
floorless squad uses a removed player and was never available, so
a higher score there is the floor working, not a defect. Neither
can ever convict, so pooling them manufactures a denominator.

The other direction needs no denominator and is the durable result:
a strictly larger pool returning a WORSE optimum convicts the search
outright, on any cell where it happens, because an exact optimiser
cannot do it.

